ctures", "targetName": "Walt Disney Pictures", "context": "Walt Disney Pictures defines the standards and practices of the animation industry through its innovative techniques and successful films."}, {"sourceSlug": "pixar-animation-studios", "sourceName": "Pixar Animation Studios", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "walt-disney-pictures", "targetName": "Walt Disney Pictures", "context": "Walt Disney Pictures collaborates with Pixar Animation Studios, leading to the creation of numerous blockbuster animated films since the 1990s."}], "places": [{"name": "Burbank, United States", "role": "Headquarters"}, {"name": "Los Angeles, United States", "role": "Cultural Center"}, {"name": "Anaheim, United States", "role": "Theme Park Location"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Walt Disney Pictures", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "walt-disney-pictures"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q191224", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walt_Disney_Pictures"], "tags": ["United States", "film production company", "Americas", "Trade Guilds & Merchant Houses", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Walt Disney Pictures left a notable mark on Modern history, documented across 64 Wikipedia editions worldwide. Key lasting impacts include: Shaped institutional landscape and community development. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Walt Disney Pictures significantly shaped the animation industry and family entertainment, influencing cultural norms and economic models in media, with films generating billions in revenue and inspiring global narratives.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-06-15T06:21:40Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27527881820", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "American film studio and a subsidiary of walt disney studios Headquartered in Walt Disney Studios. Founded 1923.", "newValue": "Walt Disney Pictures, established in 1923, is a cornerstone of American cinema and a subsidiary of Walt Disney Studios, headquartered in Burbank, California. Its founding by Walt Disney and Roy O. Disney marked the beginning of an entertainment empire that would redefine animated storytelling and family entertainment globally. The studio has played a pivotal role in the evolution of film, contributing significantly to both the animation genre and the broader landscape of motion pictures, influencing countless filmmakers and shaping popular culture through its iconic characters and narratives.

The studio's early success was cemented with the release of the first synchronized sound cartoon, "Steamboat Willie," in 1928, introducing the world to Mickey Mouse. Over the decades, Walt Disney Pictures produced groundbreaking films such as "Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs" (1937), the first full-length animated feature, and "The Lion King" (1994), which became a cultural phenomenon. The introduction of technological innovations, like the multiplane camera and digital animation, further expanded the creative horizons of animated films, allowing the studio to produce visually stunning narratives that captivated audiences worldwide.

Walt Disney Pictures' legacy is profound, as it transformed the entertainment industry, setting standards for animation and storytelling that resonate today. The influence of Disney's characters and narratives can be seen in various media and cultural contexts, inspiring generations of creators. The theme park expansions and merchandise stemming from its films further solidified Disney's cultural footprint, making it a household name across the globe. The studio has not only entertained but also shaped the values and ideals of family entertainment, which continues to evolve with each generation."}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-15T06:21:40Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27527881820", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Organizational need and institutional development"], "newValue": ["The rise of animation as a popular art form in the early 20th century created a fertile environment for Walt Disney Pictures' establishment.", "Technological advancements in film, particularly sound and color technology, enabled the studio to innovate and capture audience attention.", "The cultural demand for family-friendly entertainment in the post-World War II era positioned Disney as a leading provider of wholesome cinematic experiences."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-15T06:21:40Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27527881820", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Shaped institutional landscape and community development"], "newValue": ["Walt Disney Pictures revolutionized the animation industry, establishing benchmarks for storytelling and visual quality that persist in modern filmmaking.", "The studio's films have generated significant economic impact, contributing to the growth of the global entertainment market and related industries.", "Disney's expansion into theme parks and merchandise has created a multi-faceted entertainment empire, influencing tourism and consumer culture worldwide."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-15T06:21:40Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#